  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Strengthening Governance for Transparency and Accountability in the Belize Public Service</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Strengthening Governance for Transparency and Accountability in Belize, is a 24-month initiative designed to address the critical challenges undermining governance in Belize. By adopting a two-pronged approach, the project aims to implement a range of interventions focused on building the capacity of public servants, civil society organizations (CSOs), academia, and media, as well as strengthening the Public Service Commissions (PSC) institutional capabilities to handle cases in contravention</narrative>
  </description>
